# Auto-detected by trivy with no flag needed (default --ignorefile is
# .trivyignore) -- deliberately global rather than path-scoped, because
# trivy-action's own path-scoped `.trivyignore.yaml` + trivyignores input
# does not correctly re-apply the severity threshold before deciding the
# job's exit code when format is sarif (observed: findings well below
# CRITICAL/HIGH still failed the job). Only one ID, with a narrow,
# documented reason -- see deploy/kustomize/base/rbac.yaml for the
# rationale in context.
#
# AVD-DS-0002 (backend/Dockerfile.dev, frontend/Dockerfile.dev running as
# root) used to be ignored here on the theory that root kept the
# bind-mounted source tree and shared dependency-cache volumes writable
# without matching host UIDs. Both Dockerfiles now run as a uid-1000
# non-root user instead (chowning the mounted paths so a fresh volume
# still comes up writable), so the finding is fixed rather than accepted
# -- do not re-add it without re-litigating that decision.

# resources: ["*"] on kubemg-custom-resource-{view,edit} only ever reaches
# the enumerated, non-core API groups those ClusterRoles list (Gateway API +
# Istio) -- never the core group, where Secrets live.
AVD-KSV-0046
